  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">void get () noexcept(false);</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>Returns nothing. This function shall behave the same as the corresponding std::future function. Part of the behavior taken from the std::future is that after a call to this function the Future is not valid anymore (valid() == false).</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
